    "faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How is the Swaddle Wrap different from a muslin swaddle?",
            "answer": "<p>A muslin swaddle is a blanket you fold around baby. The Swaddle Wrap is wearable: the wrap is built in and closes with quiet fasteners, so you get a snug swaddle in seconds with no loose fabric and no folding technique to learn.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When should I stop swaddling arms-in?",
            "answer": "<p>Most guidance says to stop swaddling with arms in once your baby shows signs of starting to roll. The convertible shoulders let you switch to arms-up sleep in the same wrap, and the 1.0 TOG Sleep Bag is the next step after that. This is general information, not medical advice. For guidance specific to your baby, talk to your pediatrician.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I change a diaper without unswaddling?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The two-way zipper opens from the bottom, so you can change baby while their arms stay snug.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is TENCEL™ good for babies with sensitive skin?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. TENCEL™ Lyocell is silky smooth and naturally hypoallergenic, so there's less friction against delicate newborn skin.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
